{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":119799,"duration_api_ms":195651,"num_turns":5,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"a31094d1-4868-4a75-906a-def9dd00baaa","total_cost_usd":0.5802591,"usage":{"input_tokens":2177,"cache_creation_input_tokens":26114,"cache_read_input_tokens":76986,"output_tokens":2218,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":26114,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":12879,"outputTokens":11736,"cacheReadInputTokens":1399096,"cacheCreationInputTokens":80600,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.3122186,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2177,"outputTokens":2218,"cacheReadInputTokens":76986,"cacheCreationInputTokens":26114,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.2680405,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Verified all three amendments against the codebase. The carbonate-state fixture bug (fr-5-dde06aca) is confirmed: all five fixtures seed the stability tracker with stale pH from default chemistry after overriding DIC/alkalinity/bicarbonate without re-solving. The other two amendments are factually incorrect: the shrimp scenario tests exist and are fully implemented, and the budget helpers only handle N/C/O in mg with no alkalinity/meq paths.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-5-dde06aca","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified in crates/tank_harness/tests/e2e_shrimp_scenario_probes.rs. All five fixture functions (breeding_success_state:357, thermal_scenario_state:469, chemistry_stress_state:727, chloride_test_base_state:976, crash_mode_state:1193) call WaterState::default_for_volume_l, then override DIC/alkalinity/bicarbonate_mg_total, then call reseed_stability_tracker() without an intervening resolve_carbonate_state(). reseed_stability_tracker calls seed_from_water (biology.rs:1269) which copies water.ph into prev_ph. Since default_for_volume_l resolves carbonate state for its default DIC=20/alk=1.5 chemistry (~pH 7.3), but the overridden chemistry (e.g., DIC=5/alk=12 in breeding_success_state) would resolve to a substantially different pH, the tracker baseline is stale. The first hourly tick re-solves and corrects pH, producing a false instability signal. Adding resolve_carbonate_state after the overrides and before reseed_stability_tracker is the correct fix."},{"amendment_id":"fr-5-7b8f536e","decision":"reject","rationale":"The amendment's claims are factually incorrect. crates/tank_harness/tests/e2e_shrimp_scenario_probes.rs exists (54KB, last modified Mar 30), containing all five named shrimp scenario probes (breeding, thermal, chemistry stress, chloride, crash), the all_shrimp_probes_summary() function at line 1352, enable_probe_instrumentation() at line 119, and the breeding probe runs for 1,440 simulated hours (60 days). The amendment appears to describe a different changeset (nitrification_alkalinity.rs), not the shrimp scenario work that is actually present and complete."},{"amendment_id":"fr-5-5df4a807","decision":"reject","rationale":"The amendment misidentifies the scope of budget_helpers.rs. The Element enum (line 70-74) has exactly three variants: Nitrogen, Carbon, Oxygen. assert_budget_balanced (line 416) and assert_per_tick_balanced (line 471) only process these three elements, all in mg. They never handle alkalinity. The single 'meq' occurrence (line 67) is a doc comment explicitly stating that alkalinity in meq stays on BudgetMetric, not this enum. There is no mixed meq/mg issue because these functions have no alkalinity code path whatsoever."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"de90eea9-43a9-44e4-90b5-a644f32b99b9"}
